name: New scope filename policy is frozen and older plans retain their prefix without model work
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NODE_OPTIONS=--import=@REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/deny_provider_transport.mjs KUZUSHI_TEST_DENIED_FETCH_LOG=@ART/denied-fetch.jsonl
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_file_selection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: campaign sample-new
require-live-snap: 25 sample-new | new-fixed-plan
nav-mode:
keys: a
require-live-snap: 25 root files first, balanced directory groups | new-selection-policy
expect: One scope proposal job
expect: Boundary acceptance and scan approval remain separate.
ask: Does the new scope plan name its bounded filename selection, one-job limit and separate approval without suggesting source understanding or starting model work?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: policy-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: policy-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: policy-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: policy-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: policy-40x12
keys: NPage NPage
live-snap: policy-details-40x12
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 20 EXACT GENERATION OPTIONS | exact-options-40x12
expect: fileSelection
keys: NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage
live-snap: exact-option-tail-40x12
ask: Across six sizes and the exact-option reader, can the operator inspect the sampling policy and frozen limits using visible controls without approving or launching work?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_file_selection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME inspected
resize: 120x36
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1 NODE_OPTIONS=--import=@REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/deny_provider_transport.mjs KUZUSHI_TEST_DENIED_FETCH_LOG=@ART/denied-fetch.jsonl
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: campaign sample-legacy
require-live-snap: 25 sample-legacy | legacy-fixed-plan
nav-mode:
keys: a
require-live-snap: 25 Filename sample: recorded filename prefix | preserved-legacy-policy
expect-not: root files first
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 20 EXACT GENERATION OPTIONS | legacy-exact-options
expect-not: fileSelection
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_file_selection.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME restarted
ask: Does no-color restart preserve the authentic older plan's omitted policy and filename prefix, with both plans unchanged, zero spending and no accepted scope or started job?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
